bug_report:
gimple front-end and round trip for fails for __builtin_stdc_rotate_left
Currently with the gimple front-end format dump of optimized for:
```
void f(unsigned char   *ADDR, unsigned int nr, unsigned char mask)
{
  mask = __builtin_stdc_rotate_left (mask, nr);
  ADDR += nr >> 3;
  *ADDR &= (unsigned char) mask;
}
```

Produces:
  mask_8 = mask_6(D) r<< _1;


BUT `r<<` and `r>>` are not accepted by the gimple front-end.  That is there is no way to specify a rotate IR with the gimple front-end.  This showed up when I was trying to write a simple testcase forPR 119428.
